    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d793">

                <pb facs="0962" n="872" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg872"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.51/384: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul in Chargé of the Legation in Honduras</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Lawton</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-26T14:00:00-05:48"><hi rendition="#italic">December 26,
                                1919—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 27—11:50
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>In reply to your telegram December 15, 10 a.m. Bográn approves the plan but as
                    his term of office is so short suggested that I discuss the matter with the
                    President-elect with the result that General López<anchor n="16"
                        xml:id="d793-f1"/> asks that the Department of State suggest some person
                    suitable and cable conditions under which he could be sent to Honduras.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lawton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d793-f1" n="16" xml:id="d793-f1-content">
                <p>Gen. Rafael López Gutiérrez.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
